{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The capacitor assortment and component tester fit my breadboards, PCB supplies, and loose components: I could use them to build circuits and check parts before soldering.",
    "The signal generator fits my interest in experimenting with homemade circuits by giving me signals to test how they respond."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The heavy wire ferrules and battery lugs relate to electrical work, but their cable sizes do not fit the small battery holders and breadboard circuits I have been using.",
    "The stethoscope and grommets serve tasks I have not shown a need for, while adhesive magnets are only loosely connected to my earlier mounting supplies."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electrical components seems to have been taken as interest in electrical supplies of any size, even heavy cable connectors.",
    "My occasional purchases for mounting and practical repairs seem to have been stretched into a broader interest in unrelated craft and workshop supplies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The useful connection across my electronics purchases is small circuit assembly, experimentation, and troubleshooting, where compatible parts and component checks matter.",
    "Interest does not always mean I would choose something now: capacitors and a component tester have clear uses for me, while the oscilloscope and Zener assortment would wait for a specific project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my circuit-building interests but stretched them too far into heavy wiring and unrelated supplies, while missing the difference between useful next purchases and project-dependent interests."
}"}
